<title>GERMANY: Lower Saxon employers, unions agree job security.</title>
<headline>Lower Saxon employers, unions agree job security.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Employers and the worker's union IG Metall in the German state of Lower Saxony reached agreement on Tuesday on a new job security contract, the local branch of IG Metall said.</p>
<p>The working week can now be reduced from 35 hours to 29 hours without an accompanying wage compensation agreement, the local IG Metall head Juergen Peters said after negotiations in Hanover. The agreement runs to the end of 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
